<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malawi Congress Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1959</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a> Congress Party is a political party founded in 1959 as the successor to the banned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyasaland-african-congress">Nyasaland African Congress</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hastings-banda">Hastings Kamuzu Banda</a> it won the 1961 elections, led Nyasaland to independence as Malawi in 1964 and ruled as the sole legal party from 1966 until multiparty elections in 1994. Its leader Lazarus Chakwera won the presidency in 2020.</p></div>
